<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jigawa State</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jigawa State is a state in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, created from part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano-state">Kano State</a> in 1991, with its capital at Dutse. Largely flat savanna crossed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadejia">Hadejia</a> river, it is mainly agricultural. It includes traditional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirates</a> such as Hadejia and Gumel and the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> town of Garun Gabas, associated with the ancient kingdom of Biram.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jigawa-state.jpg" alt="Jigawa State" width="320" height="246" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Himalayan Explorer based on work by Uwe Dedering · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nigeria_Jigawa_State_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
